  "b6_answer": "3",
  "b6_reason": "LiAlH4 reduction of an isocyanide (CH3NC) gives a secondary amine (CH3NHCH3), not a primary amine; the other three routes (Hofmann degradation of the amide, and LiAlH4 reduction of the nitrile or the amide) all give primary amines.",
  "b6_working": "1: CH3CONH2 --Br2/KOH--> CH3NH2 (primary, Hofmann degradation). 2: CH3CN --LiAlH4/H3O+--> CH3CH2NH2 (primary). 3: CH3NC --LiAlH4/H3O+--> CH3NHCH3 (secondary amine, via isocyanide reduction mechanism inserting the carbon between the two N-bound carbons). 4: CH3CONH2 --LiAlH4/H3O+--> CH3CH2NH2 (primary). Only option 3 fails to give a primary amine.",
